{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the lice were on man, etc. all the dust, etc.</b> It is difficult, for it should have said ״all the dust, etc. was lice, and the lice were on man and beast.״ And it may be understood based on that which the Tosafot disagreed about in tractate Shabbat folio 12b, Rabbenu Yaakov of Orléans and Rabbenu Tam, as to what is the thing called kinnah (louse). Some of them proved from here that kinnah is the jumping [insect] whose way is to be generated from the dust of the earth; and some of them said that this [jumping insect] is called par'osh (flea), and kinnah is the white [louse] that is large [i.e. abundant] in garments, and they proved it from that which they said (Berakhot 51a): מִסְּמַרְטוּטֵי קַלְמֵי. Now according to what is said that the kinnim are the white louse, Scripture comes to remove a place of error, for the intellect would recognize this thing — that what is generated from the dust is the jumping [insect]. Therefore, if it had said ״all the dust of the earth, etc. and the lice were,״ then the simple intention would be that it is the jumping [insect]. Therefore it was stated with wisdom to say <b>and the lice were on man</b> — meaning, that which is accustomed to be on man, from him; and the generation of the plague is that its maggot would multiply and grow into the white louse on the body of man, and on beast the louse that is accustomed to be on it." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that both of them were involved in the matter: one of them is alluded to in its saying <b>and the lice were on man and beast</b> — meaning, that which is generated from man and from beast, besides the jumping [insect] for which all the dust of the earth was lice. According to this, these two species are both called kinnim, and according to this there is no proof from here for the kinnah mentioned in the words of the Sages — what it is, whether it is the white species or the jumping species, since both are called kinnah. And from now on the proofs of Rav Yosef of Orléans are no proof, and we have arrived at the ruling of Rabbenu Tam, who proved from the Talmud what it is that the Sages call kinnah — that it is the white [louse]; but the jumping [insect] the Sages designated for it a distinct name, par'osh, in order to identify the species of kinnah that they forbade on Shabbat, and so is the halakhah (Tur, Shulchan Arukh, Orach Chayim, siman 316)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:55.296918099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}